{
  "title": "test_created_at_present is flaky under heavy machine load",
  "description": "tests/test_scrape_status_page.py::TestScrapeStatusResponse::test_created_at_present \
asserts the scrape job's created_at is within 60 seconds of the client's wall \
clock. Observed a one-off failure (2026-07-12) while the API suite ran \
concurrently with two xcodebuild builds and a cargo release build; the same \
suite passed immediately before and after on an idle machine, and host and \
database clocks were in sync. Under that much load an xdist worker can \
apparently stall long enough between creating the scrape and asserting to blow \
the 60-second margin.\n\
\n\
The sanity margin is the point of the assertion (it catches populating \
created_at from the wrong column), so don't just delete it. Options: widen the \
margin (wrong-column bugs produce errors of hours or years, so even 10 minutes \
keeps the signal), or capture `now` before creating the job and assert \
created_at >= that lower bound and <= a post-request upper bound.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 4,
  "type": "chore",
  "labels": [
    "api",
    "tests",
  ],
